<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Electronic Medical Records (EMR)</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            A comprehensive, longitudinal digital health dossier that serves as the single, 
            immutable system of record for every patient interaction within your facility.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Longitudinal Health Intelligence</h2>
        <p>
            Experience radical clinical clarity with a unified patient timeline. The EMR module 
            aggregates every consultation note, laboratory result, imaging report, and 
            medication order into a single chronological view. Doctors no longer need to 
            search through disparate paper files; the entire patient history—including 
            chronic disease management trends and previous surgical interventions—is 
            available in seconds, providing the context necessary for high-quality care.
        </p>
        <p>
            Standardized ICD-10 diagnosis coding ensures that the facility's clinical data 
            is globally interoperable and ready for advanced health analytics.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Patient Safety & Alert Management</h2>
        <p>
            Protect patients through proactive surveillance. The EMR maintains a permanent, 
            high-visibility alert registry including known drug allergies, significant 
            medical conditions (e.g., Diabetes, Hypertension), and surgical risk factors. 
             these alerts are hard-wired into the prescribing and investigative 
            workflows, ensuring that clinicians are stopped if they attempt to order 
            medications or procedures that could cause harm.
        </p>
        <p>
            The system also tracks routine vaccination and immunization records, helping 
            clinics manage preventative health programs and national health campaign 
            compliance.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Digital Archival & Compliance</h2>
        <p>
            Digitize your historical records with a secure document archival sub-module. 
            Upload and link external clinical documents—such as referral letters from 
            other facilities, laboratory results from external partners, and scanned 
            physical consent forms—directly to the patient's digital dossier. Advanced 
            version control and immutable clinical audit logs ensure that the health 
            record is forensic-ready and compliant with national health records 
            legislation.
        </p>
        <p>
            Role-based access control (RBAC) ensures that sensitive patient data is only 
            visible to authorized clinical and administrative staff, maintaining 
            the highest standards of patient confidentiality.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

